 "supervisor_summary": "In round 2 the five forecasters absorbed every round-1 correction (Fed hiking, MI ~35% of revenue, post-spin net debt, H2 buyback) and converged: fair values $429-449 (mean $437), P(>=$392) 0.575-0.604. The stock is a de-rating story at ~19.4x 2027 EPS with ~13% EPS growth underwritten by buybacks. On Sep 29 the 10-yr (5.24%) and 30-yr (5.61%) hit multi-decade highs, so re-rating has no rates tailwind; I trim the upper-middle ladder by up to a point and set fair value at $432. Confidence is low, so the mean should stand; Oct 27 earnings, the Oct 28 FOMC and the Feb 2027 guide are the event risks.",
 "key_drivers": [
  "Buyback math: >$5.5B left for H2 2026 (~4.7% of shares), not yet disclosed as executed on EDGAR (no 8-K since Jul 28). This supports ~$20.2 2027 EPS; confirmation is due on the Oct 27 call",
  "Rates: the Fed hiked to 3.75-4.00% on Sep 16, an Oct 28 hike is ~2/3 priced, and on Sep 29 the 10-yr (~5.24%) and 30-yr (~5.61%) hit multi-decade highs. SPGI's ~5.2% forward earnings yield is now level with the 10-yr, which caps re-rating",
  "AI debate in Market Intelligence (~35% of revenue; Capital IQ desktop <6%). The multiple recovers only if MI subscription growth holds ~6% and API/LLM usage monetises",
  "Ratings cycle: record 2026 issuance but y/y comps flip in 2H26. The Feb 2027 guide is the key event (Feb 2026 guide: down up to 18% intraday)",
  "Indices durability: the Cboe SPX licence is extended to 2051 with a 2027 royalty reset, which removes a tail risk to the highest-quality segment"
